# caches & downloads
.probes_cache/
*.nc
*.nc4
*.csv.gz
# Anchored to the repo root. An unanchored 'data/' also matches
# src/ocean_sim/data/, which silently excluded the three loaders from every
# commit -- found by cloning to a clean directory and getting
# 'ModuleNotFoundError: No module named ocean_sim.data'.
/data/
runs/

# secrets — never commit
.env
.coopernicusmarine-credentials
credentials.json

# python
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
*.egg-info/

# notebooks
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# The notebooks themselves. Generated from workshop_notebooks.py and
# build_beginners.py, so tracking them tracked a build product of a source that is
# already in the repo. Three costs, all paid by the people who use it most: running a
# notebook modified a tracked file, so `git pull` then refused and asked for a stash;
# a notebook saved from Lab drifted from its builder (ml_03_features advertised a
# different kernelspec than the other 25); and 1.9 MB of output carried absolute temp
# paths and kernel PIDs from the machine that happened to run it last.
#
# Nothing is lost -- 'make lab' builds them, 'make notebooks' re-renders workshop_2 and
# workshop_3, 'make beginners-build' re-renders workshop_1, and CI executes them from
# the builders on every run. An attendee can now run, edit and delete a notebook freely
# and `git status` stays clean.
Workshop/workshop_*/*.ipynb

# The prefetched API responses, loose. Ignored, because they are not the artifact --
# Workshop/workshop_2/cache-archive.tar.gz is, and it is committed (see below).
# These 26 files were tracked by accident: the ignore rule read `notebooks/.cache/`,
# and when the reorg moved the tree to Workshop/ the rule stopped matching while the
# files stayed tracked. The archive is a strict superset -- 33 entries against 26, and
# it carries the Argo netCDF and SanctSound responses the tracked set was missing.
# 'make prefetch' rebuilds this directory.
Workshop/.cache/

# NOTE: Workshop/workshop_2/cache-archive.tar.gz is deliberately NOT ignored. It is
# committed, and it is what makes the workshop run with no network at all.
#
# The scratch globs below are anchored per directory on purpose. An unanchored `_*.nc`
# would also match _fetch.py and _sources.py, which are tracked source.
#
# _traps.csv was tracked too, for the same reason the loose cache was: written by a cell
# (workshop_notebooks.py:2417, notebook 10) into a directory nobody had told git to
# ignore. Running notebook 10 regenerates it.
Workshop/workshop_1/_*.nc
Workshop/workshop_2/_*.nc
Workshop/workshop_3/_*.nc
Workshop/workshop_*/_traps.csv
notebooks/data/

# macOS
.DS_Store
# AppleDouble sidecars. macOS writes a `._name` file beside anything carrying extended
# attributes, and unpacking cache-archive.tar.gz produces one for the .cache directory
# itself -- so a fresh clone was left dirty and `git pull` needed a stash. Harmless
# files, but they are not yours and you did not ask for them.
._*
probes/RESULTS.jsonl
# one-off patch scripts. Several were committed by accident, which is how
# this exists.
scripts/_p*.py
scripts/_patch*.py

# figures are regenerable from scripts/; keep the HTML so they are
# viewable without rerunning anything, but ignore the matplotlib PNGs
figures/*.png
